  "topology_summary": "Daisy-chain (line) topology: the main node connects to sub node 0 over one twisted pair, sub node 0 to sub node 1 over the next segment, and so on up to sub node 9. Exactly one main node; up to ten sub nodes. Each transceiver has a B-side (upstream, toward the main node) and an A-side (downstream, toward the next sub node).",
  "revision_history": [
    {
      "version": "A2B (AD2410)",
      "date": "First-generation",
      "description": "First A2B transceiver: single-twisted-pair daisy chain, main/sub nodes, superframe, phantom power, I2S/TDM + I2C tunneling."
    },
